hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19105","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Sufyan al-Usfuri narrated to me, from his father, from Habib ibn al-Numan al-Asadi, one of Banu Amr ibn Asad, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer, then when he finished he stood up and said: False testimony has been made equal to associating with Allah the Almighty, then he recited this verse: And avoid false speech, upright for Allah, not associating with Him."
"19106","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Shimr, from Khuraym, a man of Banu Asad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that two traits are in you, you would be you. He said: One alone suffices me. He said: You let your lower garment hang and you keep your hair abundant. He said: It is settled, by Allah, I will not do it."
"19107","Yazid informed us: al-Masudi informed us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from a man, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are six and people are four: two decisive, like for like, a good deed for ten like it, and a good deed for seven hundred. As for the two decisive: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah enters the Fire. As for like for like: whoever intends a good deed until his heart senses it and Allah knows it of him, a good deed is written for him, and whoever does an evil deed, an evil deed is written against him, and whoever does a good deed it is for ten like it, and whoever spends spending in the path of Allah, a good deed is for seven hundred. As for people: one given plenty in this world but stinted in the Hereafter, one stinted in this world but given plenty in the Hereafter, one stinted in this world and the Hereafter, and one given plenty in this world and the Hereafter."
"19108","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Shimr ibn Atiyya, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What a good man you are, O Khuraym, were it not for two traits in you. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your letting your lower garment hang and your letting your hair loose."
"19109","Marwan ibn Muawiya informed us: Sufyan ibn Ziyad informed us, from Fatik ibn Fadala, from Ayman ibn Khuraym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher and said: O people, false testimony has been made equal to associating with Allah the Almighty, three times, then he said: Avoid the filth of idols and avoid false speech."
